# src/panel.js (source) → panel.min.js (built) → panel.js (loader)

Three files, one purpose:

- **`src/panel.js`** — the **commented source of truth**. Edit this.
- **`panel.min.js`** — the **minified build** (the actual panel code that runs).
  Comments/whitespace stripped only; identifiers/syntax untouched, so it is
  semantically identical to the source. Generated by `npm run build`.
- **`panel.js`** — a tiny **loader shim**. It exists ONLY because everyone's
  installed bookmark already points at the `…/panel.js` URL. It injects
  `panel.min.js` so existing bookmarks keep working (same icon, same URL) while
  downloading the small file. **Do not put panel logic in `panel.js`.**

The installer bookmarklets in `index.html` / `mirror.html` also point at
`…/panel.js` — so old and new installs use the one canonical URL, and the loader
pulls the minified build.

## Hard rules

1. **Edit `src/panel.js`, never `panel.min.js` or `panel.js`.** `panel.min.js` is
   generated; `panel.js` is a fixed loader.
2. After any `src/panel.js` change: **`npm run build`** to regenerate
   `panel.min.js` before committing.
3. **Bump `TEP_VERSION` in `src/panel.js`** for a shipped change
   (`const TEP_VERSION = 'X.YZ';`), rebuild, and update the displayed version in
   `index.html`: `<span class="install-version" aria-label="Build">X.YZ</span>`.
   (`mirror.html` shows the build number live — no manual bump.)
4. Keep `minifyIdentifiers`/`minifySyntax` OFF in `scripts/build-min.js` so the
   served code stays semantically identical to the source; the leading license
   banner is preserved verbatim in both `panel.min.js` and the loader.

## Ship procedure (every change that goes live)

1. Edit `src/panel.js`; bump `TEP_VERSION`; update the version span in `index.html`.
2. `npm run build` (regenerates `panel.min.js`).
3. `node -c src/panel.js && node -c panel.min.js && node -c panel.js`.
4. Commit `src/panel.js`, `panel.min.js`, and any `index.html`/`mirror.html` changes.
5. Push to `main` (jsDelivr serves `@refs/heads/main`).
6. Flush the CDN — BOTH the loader and the build:
   - `purge.jsdelivr.net/gh/lucidium2000/TE-Optics@refs/heads/main/panel.js`
   - `purge.jsdelivr.net/gh/lucidium2000/TE-Optics@refs/heads/main/panel.min.js`
   The loader rarely changes, but flush it whenever it does; always flush
   `panel.min.js` since that is where the code updates land.

## Delivery model / compatibility

The bookmarklet is a small `<script src>` loader (not a giant inlined
`javascript:` URL), so the old ~500 KB URL-length limit is gone. Code only runs
on `app.thousandeyes.com` / `app.thousandeyes.us` (the source redirects
elsewhere). CSP: TE allows the jsDelivr script origin.
